The Purpose of Each Piece

* test: This is the test runner and container function. You use it to declare a new test case, name it, and gain access to browser controls (like pages, browser contexts, and cookies) via built-in objects called "fixtures".
*expect: This is the assertion engine. You use it to verify that your website is behaving correctly (e.g., checking if a button is visible, if text matches, or if a URL changed)

own word: 

• test = Your Test Case (The steps you take, like opening a page, typing text, or clicking a button).
• expect = Your Expected Result (The validation step that checks if the application matches what you actually wanted to happen).
If the expect condition is met, your test case passes ✅. If the browser shows something else, your test case fails ❌.

